!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! JOINING IT TO THE BODY IMAGE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! tests/check_mcp_body_image.py's "FIRST, LAST" (99, 184 -> 99,
! 187 once pp.185 and 186 land) and its body_page_count, NOT
! strap/mcp_image.py's MCP_IPL_PAGES: pp.15-98 and pp.99+ are two
! assemblies and merging them fails on SMCP.  This deck cannot
! edit tests/, so it says so here.
!
! >>> THIS PAGE MAKES NO HOLE AT ALL, AND I CHECKED RATHER THAN
! >>> ASSUMING IT DID. <<<  The obvious reading is that line 31's
! one-word reservation leaves 221367 empty and needs the
! reservation-span exemption.  IT DOES NOT: the card is a DRZ, and
! a DRZ's words "are all set to zero" (C22-6531 p.35), so
! strap_asm DEPOSITS a word of zeros there.  Measured on the merged
! image with this page appended:
!
!     0o221367 in prog.words        -> True (it is the image's
!                                     last word)
!     0o221367 in holes             -> False
!     0o221367 in reserved_words()  -> False
!     every_word_accounted_for      -> 0 unaccounted
!
! So the page is solid from 221350.40 to 221367.77 with nothing
! exempted, and there is no SLC skip either because there is no
! SLC.  >>> AND THIS IS WHY GLYPH CALL (4) MATTERS MORE THAN IT
! LOOKS: had the card been a DR, 221367 would be a HOLE needing
! the reservation exemption, and the merged image would hold one
! word of unspecified content instead of one word of zeros.  The Z
! is the difference, it is ink-only, and no check can see it. <<<
!
! ONE ARTIFACT OF RUNNING THE MERGE TODAY, so nobody reads it as a
! defect: with pp.185 and 186 absent, the accounting reports 55
! extra SLC-covered holes at 0o221261..0o221347 -- which is
! EXACTLY the span those two pages occupy, jumped over by this
! deck's origin SLC.  They close when pp.185 and 186 land.  With
! them absent the run still reports 0 unaccounted words.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! A TOOL FINDING, AND IT IS A CLAIM ABOUT THE REPO, NOT ABOUT MY
! PAGE -- SO IT IS CHEAP TO CHECK
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! tests/check_deck_listing_comments.py's ROW_RE requires WHITESPACE
! between the LOCATION and its second asterisk.  This deck's first
! draft wrote the block as the LOCATION column prints it,
! "221352.00* 221353.43 44", and the three marked rows then failed
! to parse as listing rows -- silently.  Measured on this deck
! alone, changing nothing but that one space:
!
!     "221352.00* ..."   ->  checks_compared = 22
!     "221352.00 * ..."  ->  checks_compared = 24
!
! and both runs printed ALL TESTS PASSED.  The tool's whole point
! is that silence can never be mistaken for verification, and its
! reach counter did exactly its job here -- but only because I
! looked at the number.  Two of my twenty-four rows (lines 8 and
! 27) were being skipped.  The rows the block still matched at
! those two locations came from the LISTING MARKS prose section,
! whose text is a STATEMENT and not a binary, so BINARY_RE
! correctly discarded them and nothing was compared at all.
!
! >>> AND FOUR LANDED DECKS ARE LOSING ROWS THE SAME WAY.  I
! >>> MEASURED IT RATHER THAN SAYING "other decks may be". <<<
! Five decks in decks/ write a location-column asterisk with no
! space.  Re-running scan() on each, with nothing changed but that
! space inserted:
!
!     p.88    compared 42 -> 44
!     p.96    compared 41 -> 44
!     p.97    compared 26 -> 27
!     p.125   compared 53 -> 56
!     p.166   compared 44 -> 44   (its marks are in prose, not the
!                                  block; nothing lost)
!
! NINE ROWS across the corpus, and ZERO of them mismatch once they
! are compared -- so this is lost REACH, not a hidden defect.  I
! cannot edit tests/, so: either ROW_RE should allow "LOC*" with no
! space (a fifth house layout), or the workflow doc should tell
! transcribers to write "LOC *".
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE PRINTED LISTING, AS READ
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!   line  1*                                                       ****************************************************
!   line  2*                                                       -***********   EOP TEST FOR SEOP TYPE I/O   ***********-
!   line  3*                                                       ****************************************************
!   line  4*                                                           CALLING SEQUENCE  **  SIC,K EOP R<record mark>B,K SEOP T
!   line  5*                                                       (empty comment card)
!   line  6   221350.40  000036.03 02                    K SEOP T  LCI,1,K REP
!   line  7   221351.00  000000.00 8E 221367.21 00                 CCW,0.0($14),K WS
!   line  8   221352.00 * 221353.43 44                              BZEKJZ,$+1.32
!   line  9   221352.40  221351.02 48                              CB,1,$-1.32
!   line 10   221353.00  221300.10 00                              B,K REJT
!   line 11   221353.40  221367.23 80 006000.20 50                 L(BU,6),K WS.19          -TEST STATUS INDICATORS
!   line 12   221354.40  221354.74 C2                    K EOP R   BRZ,$                    -IF NONE ON, ALLS WELL
!   line 13   221355.00  221367.30 80 221350.74 02                 BB,K WS.24,K SEOP T      -IF SEOP BIT ON, LOOP
!   line 14   221356.00  750000.00 80 406000.02 70                 CI0001(BU,6),(.5,2)111101 -TEST IF ONLY CS IS ON
!   line 15   221357.00  221354.74 C2                              BRZ,K EOP R              -IF SO, ALLS WELL
!   line 16   221357.40  221367.25 80 221365.34 00                 BZB,KWS.21,ZTSEOP
!   line 17   221360.40  221364.43 D0                              SVA,$1,RSVRTN
!   line 18   221361.00  221313.40 80                              SIC,KCBJR
!   line 19   221361.40  221302.50 00                              B,KCLEAR
!   line 20   221362.00  221354.43 B0                              LVE,$1,KEOPR
!   line 21   221362.40  220046.03 04                              KVI,$1,ZLOCXX
!   line 22   221363.00  000000.32 C3                              BXE,($1)
!   line 23   221363.40  217624.43 04                              KVI,$1,KKMODE
!   line 24   221364.00  000000.32 C3                              BXE,($1)
!   line 25   221364.40  221364.43 01                    RSVRTN    LVI,$1,$
!   line 26   221365.00  221274.26 4A                    ZTSEOP    CBZ,$11,KSOS
!   line 27   221365.40 * 221313.40 80                              SIC,K CBJ R
!   line 28   221366.00  221302.50 00                              B,K CLEAR                -CLEAR CONTROL WORD FOR RETRY
!   line 29   221366.40  221263.10 00                              B,K RETRY
!   line 30                                                        CNOP
!   line 31   221367.00 * 000001.00                       KWS       DRZ(N),(1)
!
