!SYM KSEOPT 221350.40
!SYM KEOPR  221354.40
!SYM RSVRTN 221364.40
!SYM ZTSEOP 221365.00
!SYM KWS    221367.00
!
!CHECK 221350.40 | 000036.03 02 | line 6 K SEOP T LCI,1,K REP -- K REP is a COUNT of 30 (p.125's landed SYN), not an address, so 000036 is the immediate 0o36 = 30 itself and this row checks the value outright; .03 is 2J+1 = 3 for J=1. Five other pages print the identical half word for the identical card (K NET, K CBJ, K CLEAR, K SEQUL, K K LOOP all do "LCI,1,K REP")
!CHECK 221351.00 | 000000.00 8E 221367.21 00 | line 7 CCW,0.0($14),K WS -- 8E's low nibble is index $14 on the all-zero first address; the second word's 0o21 is NOT a bit offset but instruction bits 50-55, the CCW op 0b1000 followed by the leading 1 of the pocket card's 10000 literal, so this row reads K WS's WORD (221367) and nothing below it. K WS's .00 comes from line 31's own LOCATION column
!CHECK 221352.00 | 221353.43 44 | line 8 BZEKJZ,$+1.32 -- $ is this row's 221352.00 and "1.32" is a BARE decimal offset, so +1 word +32 bits = +1.40 octal = 221353.40, printing 0o40 OR the 0o03 indicator as 0o43. The deck hands the assembler the printed mnemonic and it is accepted; the byte 44 is the whole of what checks the Z's. This row carries the first location-column asterisk
!CHECK 221352.40 | 221351.02 48 | line 9 CB,1,$-1.32 -- the MINUS counterpart of line 8 and its control: $ is 221352.40, less 1 word 32 bits = 221351.00, and .02 is 2J = 2 for J=1 against line 8's branch-indicator 0o43. Two rows, one page, the same "1.32" decimal offset read in both directions
!CHECK 221353.00 | 221300.10 00 | line 10 B,K REJT -- target+0o10; bit offset unobservable. K REJT is p.125's landed SYN at 221300.0 and the volume OCR's defining card reads "221300.00 K REJT LVI,14,S REJ -I/O COMMAND REJECTED"; five other pages print this identical half word
!CHECK 221353.40 | 221367.23 80 006000.20 50 | line 11 L(BU,6),K WS.19 -TEST STATUS INDICATORS -- >>> A VFL OPERAND IS BIT-EXACT, so this row READS 221367.23: line 31 prints K WS's LOCATION as 221367.00 and 0o23 = 19 decimal, which is the printed ".19" as a BARE DECIMAL offset. The decimal-to-octal conversion is therefore checked outright and not assumed. The second word is the (BU,6) dds 0o006000 with offset 0 and the L code 20 50. >>> THE DECK WRITES "KWS.19" CLOSED UP; THE PAGE PRINTS "K WS.19" WITH A BLANK, which strap_asm refuses -- see WHAT HAD TO BE SUBSTITUTED
!CHECK 221354.40 | 221354.74 C2 | line 12 K EOP R BRZ,$ -IF NONE ON, ALLS WELL -- $ is this row's own 221354.40, so 0o40 OR the BRZ indicator 0o34 = 0o74. This is the label five landed decks SYN at 221354.40 and several of them with a SIC, so the row is also the page's own statement of its origin
!CHECK 221355.00 | 221367.30 80 221350.74 02 | line 13 BB,K WS.24,K SEOP T -IF SEOP BIT ON, LOOP -- the first address is a VFL-class bit address and reads K WS to the bit: 0o30 = 24 decimal, the printed ".24". The second is THIS page's line 6 label at 221350.40, printing 0o40 OR 0o34 = 0o74 with the BB byte 02, so the row pins the page's first located row from eleven half-words later. >>> "KWS.24" IS WRITTEN CLOSED UP; THE PAGE PRINTS "K WS.24"
!CHECK 221356.00 | 750000.00 80 406000.02 70 | line 14 CI0001(BU,6),(.5,2)111101 -TEST IF ONLY CS IS ON -- the immediate 111101 is LEFT-JUSTIFIED in A24 and prints as 0o750000, which is 0o75 = 111101 in the top six bits: the word itself re-states the six characters, which is how the last one was settled (it prints as a C and a radix-2 literal cannot hold one -- see GLYPH CALL 1). The second word is the (BU,6) dds with the connective code 02 70
!CHECK 221357.00 | 221354.74 C2 | line 15 BRZ,K EOP R -IF SO, ALLS WELL -- byte for byte the SAME HALF WORD as line 12, which is what makes the pair useful: line 12 reaches it through "$" and line 15 through the symbol, so the label and the counter agree independently
!CHECK 221357.40 | 221367.25 80 221365.34 00 | line 16 BZB,KWS.21,ZTSEOP -- 0o25 = 21 decimal reads K WS to the bit a third time, with a third different offset (.19, .24, .21 all against one symbol); Z TSEOP is THIS page's line 26 at 221365.00, printing 0o34 with bit 32 CLEAR, which is what distinguishes it from a .40. The page prints this name CLOSED UP, so no substitution here
!CHECK 221360.40 | 221364.43 D0 | line 17 SVA,$1,RSVRTN -- R SVRTN is THIS page's line 25 at 221364.40; 0o43 is 0o40 OR 2J+1 = 3 for J=1, so bit 32 is SET and the .40 is checked. The byte D0 is the same SVA byte printed p.184 line 21 prints
!CHECK 221361.00 | 221313.40 80 | line 18 SIC,KCBJR -- AN SIC CARRIES ITS OPERAND'S FULL 24-BIT BIT ADDRESS, so this row READS K CBJ R at 221313.40 to the bit. printed p.184 line 24 is the same card and prints the same half word, and printed p.186 line 9 is the defining card. Line 27 is the same statement again with the name spelled "K CBJ R"
!CHECK 221361.40 | 221302.50 00 | line 19 B,KCLEAR -- K CLEAR is landed at 221302.40 and 0o40 OR 0o10 = 0o50 checks bit 32. Repeated verbatim on line 28 with the blanks in
!CHECK 221362.00 | 221354.43 B0 | line 20 LVE,$1,KEOPR -- the SAME symbol as lines 12 and 15 through a THIRD operation: 0o43 is 0o40 OR 2J+1 for J=1 against the branches' 0o74, so the two operation classes agree on bit 32 and on nothing below it. The byte B0 is LVE's
!CHECK 221362.40 | 220046.03 04 | line 21 KVI,$1,ZLOCXX -- Z LOCXX is DEFINED by printed p.159 line 39 at 220046.00; .03 is 2J+1 = 3 for J=1 with bit 32 CLEAR, which is what confirms the landed ".00". A KVI is index-class, so only bit 32 shows and the deck's SYN says so
!CHECK 221363.00 | 000000.32 C3 | line 22 BXE,($1) -- no address at all, so the whole half word is the operation: 0o32 and the byte C3. Line 24 is the identical card and its control
!CHECK 221363.40 | 217624.43 04 | line 23 KVI,$1,KKMODE -- K K MODE is landed at 217624.40 by pp.151/152/154/183; 0o43 is 0o40 OR 3, so bit 32 is SET here where line 21's Z LOCXX has it clear, and the two KVI rows are each other's control on that bit
!CHECK 221364.00 | 000000.32 C3 | line 24 BXE,($1) -- the same word as line 22, printed twice on one page from the same statement
!CHECK 221364.40 | 221364.43 01 | line 25 RSVRTN LVI,$1,$ -- $ is this row's own 221364.40, so 0o43 = 0o40 OR 2J+1 for J=1 is self-referential; what makes it a real check is line 17's SVA, which reaches the SAME 221364.43 through the SYMBOL. Byte 01 is LVI's against the SVA's D0
!CHECK 221365.00 | 221274.26 4A | line 26 ZTSEOP CBZ,$11,KSOS -- 0o26 = 2J = 22 decimal for J=11 with bit 32 CLEAR, so K SOS is at 221274.00 (p.125's landed SYN, and the volume OCR's p.185 defining card); 4A's low nibble is the index 11. >>> THE "O" OF KSOS IS AN OPEN ROUND GLYPH AND I DID NOT SETTLE IT -- see WHAT I COULD NOT SETTLE (A). This check passes either way, which is exactly why that note exists
!CHECK 221365.40 | 221313.40 80 | line 27 SIC,K CBJ R -- the SAME CARD as line 18 with the name spelled with its blanks in, compiling the identical half word. Two spellings of one symbol on one page, and an SIC both times, so K CBJ R's 221313.40 is read to the bit twice. This row carries the second location-column asterisk
!CHECK 221366.00 | 221302.50 00 | line 28 B,K CLEAR -CLEAR CONTROL WORD FOR RETRY -- the same half word as line 19 with the blanks in
!CHECK 221366.40 | 221263.10 00 | line 29 B,K RETRY -- target+0o10; bit offset unobservable. K RETRY is the one external whose defining page has not landed: the volume OCR of printed p.185 line 12 prints "221263.00 K RETRY LX,0,S IO INS($12)" and p.186 line 9 prints this identical half word for the same symbol

KREP    SYN(BU,18), 30              ! dds (BU,18) from printed p.185 line 27,
                                     !   which PRINTS the defining card
                                     !   "K REP SYN(BU,18),30" (dds column
                                     !   BU,22 ,10 = length 0o22 = 18).
                                     !   Added 2026-11-02: the merged body
                                     !   image refused without it.                      ! landed: p.125 "A COUNT, not an address"
KREJT   SYN, (8)221300.0             ! landed: p.125; line 10 B, half word only
KSOS    SYN, (8)221274.0             ! landed: p.125; line 26 CBZ, half word only; SPELLING OPEN, see (A)
KCBJR   SYN, (8)221313.40            ! landed: pp.125/126/184; lines 18 and 27 are SICs -- BIT-EXACT
KCLEAR  SYN, (8)221302.40            ! landed: pp.125/126/184; lines 19 and 28 print 221302.50
KKMODE  SYN, (8)217624.40            ! landed: pp.151/152/154/183; line 23 KVI
ZLOCXX  SYN, (8)220046.0             ! p.159 line 39 DEFINES it, with the dds; line 21 KVI, half word only
KRETRY  SYN, (8)221263.0             ! p.185's OCR'd defining card; p.185 NOT YET LANDED -- see EXTERNALS

        SLC, (8)221350.40            ! NOT PRINTED.  The counter arrives here from
                                     ! p.186; the origin is CHECKED by the merge --
                                     ! see THE JOIN, BOTH WAYS
KSEOPT  LCI,1,K REP                  ! line  6   printed name "K SEOP T"
        CCW,0.0($14),K WS            ! line  7   blanked name as a BARE operand: accepted
        BZEKJZ,$+1.32                ! line  8 * location-column asterisk
        CB,1,$-1.32                  ! line  9
        B,K REJT                     ! line 10
        L(BU,6),KWS.19               ! line 11   >>> PRINTED "K WS.19"; blank refused <<<
KEOPR   BRZ,$                        ! line 12   printed name "K EOP R"
        BB,KWS.24,K SEOP T           ! line 13   >>> PRINTED "K WS.24"; blank refused <<<
        CI0001(BU,6),(.5,2)111101    ! line 14   last digit prints as a C; see GLYPH CALL 1
        BRZ,K EOP R                  ! line 15
        BZB,KWS.21,ZTSEOP            ! line 16   the page prints "KWS.21" closed up
        SVA,$1,RSVRTN                ! line 17
        SIC,KCBJR                    ! line 18
        B,KCLEAR                     ! line 19
        LVE,$1,KEOPR                 ! line 20
        KVI,$1,ZLOCXX                ! line 21
        BXE,($1)                     ! line 22
        KVI,$1,KKMODE                ! line 23
        BXE,($1)                     ! line 24
RSVRTN  LVI,$1,$                     ! line 25
ZTSEOP  CBZ,$11,KSOS                 ! line 26
        SIC,K CBJ R                  ! line 27 * location-column asterisk
        B,K CLEAR                    ! line 28
        B,K RETRY                    ! line 29
        CNOP                         ! line 30   emits NOTHING: 221367.00 is already
                                     ! word aligned.  The listing prints no location
                                     ! and no binary for it, so it writes no !CHECK
KWS     DRZ(N),(1)                   ! line 31 * one word; the Z and the N are INK ONLY
